<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to November 6, as released by the Bank of Japan on Thursday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.37 (0.38)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.45 (0.47)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  0.95 (1.00)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.33 (0.33)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.40 (0.42)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  0.90 (0.95)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.28 (0.29)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.34 (0.37)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.25 (0.25)	 three years  0.85 (0.90)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Nov 05 - Nov 08:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.48 (0.48)   120-150 days  0.52 (0.52)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.50 (0.50)   150-180 days  0.53 (0.55)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.50 (0.50)   180-360 days  0.55 (0.55)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.52 (0.52)   over 360 days 0.70 (0.62)</p>
